dsh-acp-commands
================

This repository contains a modified copy of the ACP bridge published by
DeepSeek as `@deepseek-ai/dsh-acp`, which is MIT licensed.

  Upstream package : @deepseek-ai/dsh-acp@0.2.1-rc.2
  Upstream source  : https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
                     (packages/acp/acp)
  Upstream license : MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek

The file `lib/index.js` is that package's compiled `lib/index.js`, patched in
four places. `docs/patches.md` documents each hook with exact snippets.

Modifications, Copyright (c) 2026 Gennady Artamonov:

  1. Plugin identity and dependency set: the plugin is named `acp-commands` and
     additionally injects the `commands` service.
  2. Command advertisement: `session/update` with `available_commands_update`
     after `session/new`, after `session/resume`, and on `commands/change`,
     scheduled so the triggering response reaches the client first.
  3. Slash dispatch: a prompt that is exactly one text block starting a
     registered command is executed through `ctx.commands.execute()` instead of
     becoming a model turn; the settled text is returned as an
     `agent_message_chunk`.
  4. Fallback: unknown slash input and prompts carrying non-text blocks keep the
     original model path.

Everything else in `lib/index.js` — session lifecycle, model and reasoning
config, MCP mounting, permission requests, persistence, teardown — is upstream
code, unchanged.

